From: Construct <release@constructlinux.org>
Subject: authPrompt: Cancel a pending verification when the prompt finishes without one

The unlock dialog finishes its prompt when the shield is deactivated,
and not only after a successful verification: logind's Unlock signal
(loginctl unlock-session) and the shield's own deactivate() do it with
the prompt still waiting for the password. finish() then cleared the
user verifier without cancelling it, so GDM never heard the
reauthentication was over: its session kept the conversation, and the
gdm-password worker waiting for the answer stayed alive with its pidfd,
its socket pair and its connection in the session's worker, until this
process asked for another prompt and replaced the request, or for good.
Measured over three lock, prompt and deactivate cycles: one worker and
5 file descriptors left after each unlock, replaced at the next prompt.

Cancel the verifier when the prompt finishes without a successful
verification: GDM resets the session and stops its conversations, as
it does when the person cancels the prompt.

--- a/js/gdm/authPrompt.js
+++ b/js/gdm/authPrompt.js
@@ -1047,16 +1047,26 @@
     }
 
     finish(onComplete) {
-        if (!this._userVerifier.hasPendingMessages) {
-            this._userVerifier.clear();
+        // Finished without a verification - the session unlocked through
+        // logind, the shield dropped - a conversation still waiting for its
+        // answer must be cancelled, or GDM keeps it, a password worker with
+        // it, until this process asks for another.
+        const done = () => {
+            if (this.verificationStatus === AuthPromptStatus.VERIFICATION_SUCCEEDED)
+                this._userVerifier.clear();
+            else
+                this._userVerifier.cancel();
             onComplete();
+        };
+
+        if (!this._userVerifier.hasPendingMessages) {
+            done();
             return;
         }
 
         const signalId = this._userVerifier.connect('no-more-messages', () => {
             this._userVerifier.disconnect(signalId);
-            this._userVerifier.clear();
-            onComplete();
+            done();
         });
     }
 
